# Rank 1970 / CVE-2021-21665: the XebiaLabs XL Deploy Jenkins plugin's
# credential validation endpoint resolved a stored credential by the
# caller-supplied credentialsId and opened a connection to the
# caller-supplied server URL, and because the method imposed no POST
# requirement a request forged against a logged-in browser session could
# drive the connection with attacker-chosen target and credential
# (CWE-352; SECURITY-1982, Jenkins advisory 2021-06-10).
#
# Credential.DescriptorImpl.doValidateCredential took deployitServerUrl,
# secondaryServerUrl and credentialsId from @QueryParameter, called
# lookupSystemCredentials(credentialsId), and passed the resolved secret
# straight into validateConnection(serverUrl, proxyUrl,
# credentials.getPassword().getPlainText()). The method carried a
# Permission.CREATE check — the advisory's CVE-2021-21664 facet calls that
# the wrong permission — but no @RequirePOST, so the endpoint stayed
# reachable through forged GET requests.
#
# Pool flag nocommit is wrong: 79ae204d2e6 exists and reads fine, but it is
# only the partial fix (7.5.9) that introduced the wrong-permission state.
# The CSRF remediation — @RequirePOST plus Jenkins.ADMINISTER in place of
# Permission.CREATE — lands in 0dbf787f1786 (10.0.2), so the row's SHA is
# repointed there and the revision pair is 0dbf787^ against 0dbf787.
#
# FIXED. code.JenkinsRemoteValidationMissingPostPermission carries
# this weakness (CWE_352 first among its three) and VYQL-RF-023
# reports it for the doTest*/doCheck* connection-test family. The existing
# bindings in that family key on each plugin's own connection call and
# require that no checkPermission exists at all, which cannot fire here:
# this method checks a permission, just the wrong one, and the forgery
# window is the missing POST requirement. Added a sibling binding keyed on
# the same doValidate*/doTest*/doCheck* + @QueryParameter + a stored
# credential's plaintext reaching a connection call, cleared by
# @POST/@RequirePOST, not by the presence of a permission check: a checked
# permission does not stop a cross-site request.
#
# Deliberately not negated on checkPermission: the advisory's own fix shape
# (correct permission, still no POST) would be re-reported as clean.
#
# verify_current_expected: current-behavior

test "rank1970: credential validation endpoint drives a connection without a POST requirement"
  lang java
  file Credential.java
  expect_review code.JenkinsRemoteValidationMissingPostPermission
  code
  ```
  public class Credential {
      public static class DescriptorImpl extends Descriptor<Credential> {

          public FormValidation doValidateCredential(@QueryParameter String deployitServerUrl,
                                                     @QueryParameter String secondaryServerUrl,
                                                     @QueryParameter String credentialsId) throws IOException {
              Jenkins.getInstance().checkPermission(Permission.CREATE);
              try {
                  String serverUrl = Strings.isNullOrEmpty(secondaryServerUrl) ? deployitServerUrl : secondaryServerUrl;
                  StandardUsernamePasswordCredentials credentials = lookupSystemCredentials(credentialsId);
                  if (credentials == null) {
                      return FormValidation.error("Could not find credential with id '%s'", credentialsId);
                  }
                  return validateConnection(serverUrl, proxyUrl, credentials.getUsername(), credentials.getPassword().getPlainText());
              } catch (Exception e) {
                  return FormValidation.error("! %s", e.getMessage());
              }
          }
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1970: credential validation requiring POST and administer is clean"
  lang java
  file Credential.java
  reject_review code.JenkinsRemoteValidationMissingPostPermission
  code
  ```
  public class Credential {
      public static class DescriptorImpl extends Descriptor<Credential> {

          @RequirePOST
          public FormValidation doValidateCredential(@QueryParameter String deployitServerUrl,
                                                     @QueryParameter String secondaryServerUrl,
                                                     @QueryParameter String credentialsId) throws IOException {
              Jenkins.getInstance().checkPermission(Jenkins.ADMINISTER);
              try {
                  String serverUrl = Strings.isNullOrEmpty(secondaryServerUrl) ? deployitServerUrl : secondaryServerUrl;
                  StandardUsernamePasswordCredentials credentials = lookupSystemCredentials(credentialsId);
                  if (credentials == null) {
                      return FormValidation.error("Could not find credential with id '%s'", credentialsId);
                  }
                  return validateConnection(serverUrl, proxyUrl, credentials.getUsername(), credentials.getPassword().getPlainText());
              } catch (Exception e) {
                  return FormValidation.error("! %s", e.getMessage());
              }
          }
      }
  }
  ```
